  "id": "29",
  "name": "Manufacture of motor vehicles, trailers and semi-trailers",
  "section": "C",
  "summary": "Car, truck and parts makers write about AI mostly as driver assistance and automated driving (ADAS, SAE levels, robotaxis, end-to-end driving models), the software-defined vehicle, intelligent cockpits and over-the-air updates, plus the chips, sensors and training compute behind them. In operations AI appears in smart factories, quality inspection, virtual validation and humanoid robot pilots. Risk and regulation sections cover safety investigations and liability for assisted driving, UNECE and NCAP rules, vehicle cyber security and data rules, dependence on chip suppliers and shortages, and competition for software talent.",
